    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All **70 tests pass** \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`. The V2 checkpoints (Cp52/53/55/56/57/60) and the region/locality/segment tests (Cp17/30/42/35/46) are all green, along with the rest of the suite.\n\n## What I changed\n\n**Identity derivation \u2014 V2 tag mixed in so every identifier changes and no V1 value recurs:**\n- `OwnerRegion.java` \u2014 added `VERSION_TAG = \"V2\"` and `identityRegion(owner)` returning the plain region plus the tag (e.g. `NSWV2`). Since it contains a digit, a V2 memberId can never equal a plain-region V1 one. `of(owner)` (plain region) is unchanged.\n- `AssignMemberId.java` \u2014 the memberId's REGION prefix now uses `OwnerRegion.identityRegion(...)`.\n- `AssignHouseholdId.java` \u2014 hashes `'V2'|lastName|postcode` (was `lastName|postcode`).\n- `OwnerIdentityKey.java` \u2014 hashes `'V2'|telephone|email|soundex(lastName)`; equality semantics (duplicate detection) preserved.\n\n**Response shape:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 removed top-level `memberId`/`householdId`/`identityKey`; added a nested `OwnerIdentity` schema (those three) referenced as `identity`, plus a top-level integer `apiVersion`. Rewrote the `locality` description.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 maps `identity` (new `identity(owner)` builder) and `apiVersion = 2`; `locality(owner)` now derives the **plain** region directly via `OwnerRegion.of` instead of reading the (now V2-tagged) memberId prefix \u2014 so `locality`/`timezone`/owner-segment region stay plain `NSW`. The owner segment is recomputed from that plain region.\n\n**Audit:**\n- `AuditOwnerCreated.java` \u2014 structured event moved to schema version 2, adding `\"schemaVersion\":2`; still carries the ownerId and the (now V2) memberId.\n\nThe audit logs confirm the split: `memberId=NSWV227786E13D53` (V2 inside the identifier) while `locality` reads back plain `NSW`. Request fields (`OwnerFields`) were untouched.",
