    "probe_text": "My direct read of the pipeline is confirmed by the background exploration, with one nuance worth adding:\n\n- **The DTO's own bean-validation annotations are *not* enforced.** `ValidateOwnerFields` binds the body as `@RequestBody OwnerFieldsDto` **without `@Valid`**, so the JSR-380 constraints declared on `OwnerFieldsDto` (`@NotNull`, `@Pattern`, `@Size`, `@Email`, etc.) never run. All field validation on this endpoint is the imperative logic in steps 2\u20133 (`ValidateOwnerFields` + `ValidatePostcode`) \u2014 which is why, e.g., the disposable-email and region-range rules exist in code rather than as annotations.\n\nTwo smaller corrections to my earlier phrasing, from the class internals:\n- The `identityKey` (step 8) also folds in a `\"V2\"` version tag and the email \u2014 the full hashed input is `V2|normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)`.\n- `CheckHouseholdUnique` / `OwnerHouseholdConflictException` classes exist in the tree but are **not** wired into `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 the former separate household-duplicate 409 was consolidated into the single identity check (step 8).\n\nEverything else in the ordered list stands: one `OWNER_ADMIN` guard, an idempotency short-circuit, four rejecting validations (400/400/409/429), the identity 409, then the build + eight assign/enrich side-effects, save, idempotency registration, audit + notify logging, and the 201 response."
